    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="1119" n="1087" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg1087"/>

                <head>591. Letter From the Secretary of State to the Secretary of Defense
                        (Gates)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d591-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-10-14"><hi rendition="#italic">October 14,
                        1960</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Tom</hi>: I have your letter of October 4,
                        1960<anchor n="2" xml:id="d591-f2"/> in which you refer to Castro’s recent
                    statments indicating that he may unilaterally denounce the treaty under which we
                    maintain the Base at Guantanamo. In your letter you informed me that you have
                    reaffirmed your instructions to the Joint Chiefs of Staff that we hold this Base
                    against all forms of harassment, including armed attack.</p>
                <p>I appreciate your assurance that you do not anticipate taking any provocative
                    steps, and I am in complete agreement that your contingency plans should be
                    prepared to include defensive actions beyond the perimeter of the Base should
                    this be required to meet armed attack. I am sure you will agree, however, that a
                    decision of this nature should be made by the President.</p>
                <p>It should, of course, also be borne in mind in planning against the contingency
                    of an armed attack upon the Guantanamo Base that such an action by the Cuban
                    Government would call for the immediate invocation by this Government of Article
                    3 of the Inter-American Treaty of Reciprocal Assistance.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d591-f3"/> As you know, this article concerns the responsibilities
                    of all the American States when an armed attack upon one of them occurs.</p>
                <p>With warmest personal regards,</p>
                <p>Most sincerely,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Chris</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d591-f4"
                        /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
